ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20261, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016mH26G4X4pnvHQCwmfuNCg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20261, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013K3VibUs9demG4gwT1Dmi4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20561, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013K3VibUs9demG4gwT1Dmi4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20561, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013K3VibUs9demG4gwT1Dmi4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25253, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01BQBYGcd9BFa9Lnm6pbsWKT", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 went to production, checkout-api started failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error: us-east moved to v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished successfully. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look into why v2.3.1 was promoted to production even though its RC failed in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55853, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BQBYGcd9BFa9Lnm6pbsWKT", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55853, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BQBYGcd9BFa9Lnm6pbsWKT", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58703, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DuTx2rimHVptuizaFx3brD", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59003, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DuTx2rimHVptuizaFx3brD", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59003, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DuTx2rimHVptuizaFx3brD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 65036, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that. This didn't need approval, since the approval rule only applies to versions that have never been healthy.\n- The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. us-east moved to v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I checked where each region stood and tried once more, which worked.\n- All regions now run v2.3.0. The service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2) is open for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the stalled first attempt and the current state.\n- The request to create it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had already gone through, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- It lists three things to follow up on:\n  - why v2.3.1 failed\n  - what caused the orchestrator error\n  - why v2.3.1 reached production after its release candidate failed in staging", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VdQVnXGAiX2zSLVDrYmF3t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01A2hPBG7x83WhTZXXdkoD53", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019vKYYVv2iRgPusSZyRysnU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01166Um8MAMxfKTLyfZFa3L1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TAXNAVua8ofPHrxQaBVCfz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016mH26G4X4pnvHQCwmfuNCg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013K3VibUs9demG4gwT1Dmi4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BQBYGcd9BFa9Lnm6pbsWKT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 went to production, checkout-api started failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error: us-east moved to v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished successfully. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look into why v2.3.1 was promoted to production even though its RC failed in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DuTx2rimHVptuizaFx3brD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that. This didn't need approval, since the approval rule only applies to versions that have never been healthy.\n- The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. us-east moved to v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I checked where each region stood and tried once more, which worked.\n- All regions now run v2.3.0. The service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2) is open for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the stalled first attempt and the current state.\n- The request to create it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had already gone through, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- It lists three things to follow up on:\n  - why v2.3.1 failed\n  - what caused the orchestrator error\n  - why v2.3.1 reached production after its release candidate failed in staging", "type": "text"}]}]}